---
source: crates/mori-checker/src/tests.rs
description: "Code:\n\nprofile \"moriarty-beta/1\";\nagreement Amm {\n  domain Preview = { id: \"preview\", chain: \"midnight\", network: \"preview\" };\n  asset USD = { domain: Preview, id: \"usd\", scale: 2, representation: \"native\" };\n  asset GOLD = { domain: Preview, id: \"gold\", scale: 3, representation: \"native\" };\n  asset EUR = { domain: Preview, id: \"eur\", scale: 2, representation: \"native\" };\n  account alice = { domain: Preview, id: \"alice\" };\n  pool amm = { domain: Preview, id: \"amm\", assets: [USD, GOLD] };\n  const swap = amm.swap_exact_input(\n    pool: amm,\n    owner: alice,\n    input: 10 USD,\n    output_asset: EUR,\n    net_floor: 1 GOLD,\n    fee_cap: 0.1 EUR,\n  );\n}\n"
---
mori::check::not_in_pool

  × `EUR` is not one of the pool `amm`'s assets.
    ╭─[test.mori:13:19]
 12 │     input: 10 USD,
 13 │     output_asset: EUR,
    ·                   ─┬─
    ·                    ╰── not in the pool
 14 │     net_floor: 1 GOLD,
    ╰────
  help: A pool only trades the assets listed in its `assets` field.

mori::check::wrong_asset

  × `net_floor` must be a `EUR` amount because it is measured in
  │ `output_asset`, but it is a `GOLD` amount.
    ╭─[test.mori:14:16]
 13 │     output_asset: EUR,
 14 │     net_floor: 1 GOLD,
    ·                ───┬──
    ·                   ╰── a `GOLD` amount
 15 │     fee_cap: 0.1 EUR,
    ╰────

mori::check::wrong_asset

  × `fee_cap` must be a `USD` amount because fees are paid in the `input`
  │ asset, but it is a `EUR` amount.
    ╭─[test.mori:15:14]
 14 │     net_floor: 1 GOLD,
 15 │     fee_cap: 0.1 EUR,
    ·              ───┬───
    ·                 ╰── a `EUR` amount
 16 │   );
    ╰────
